The instruction_following_eval package is adapted from Google Research
(Apache License 2.0). Sentence and word counts use the same rules as that
checker, with the NLTK punkt download replaced by the regex splitter that
already ships in instructions_util.py. Scores on number_sentences can differ
slightly from a punkt-based run.

The BFCL ast_checker is adapted from the Berkeley Function Calling Leaderboard
in ShishirPatil/gorilla (Apache License 2.0). This copy scores the Python
prompting track. Java, JavaScript, and multi-turn execution are not included.

The BBH chain-of-thought prompts in third_party/bbh_cot are the published
cot-prompts from suzgunmirac/BIG-Bench-Hard. BIG-Bench itself is Apache
License 2.0. The canary line is kept in each file and stripped before the
prompt is sent to the model. The 3-object, 5-object, and 7-object files for
logical deduction and tracking shuffled objects are identical upstream.
